You found the first hidden file. Nicely spotted.

You know that a dot at the start of a name hides a file from "ls". The
same trick works for whole folders. There is a folder here that the
normal "ls" does not show.

Next clue: "cat .secrets/vault.txt"
   ___   ___   ___
  | o | | p | | ! |   vault open
   ---   ---   ---

You reached the end of the hunt. To open this folder you had to know that:
  - a name starting with "." stays hidden from "ls",
  - the files and folders are still there, you just need the path,
  - "cat" reads any file as long as you give it the right path.

That is exactly the kind of curiosity this shell was built to reward.

If you are a recruiter and you made it here: thanks for exploring. The
path you just took (reading code, following clues, working out how the
tools behave under the hood) is how I like to work.

Get in touch: "cat contacts.txt"
